      "message": "SkSL can now support sk_SecondaryFragColor on top of SPIR-V when hardware supports this. I can successfully see the dual src blend shaders produced within GMs without negatively impacting the visual output.\n\nAccording to gpuinfo.org, about 50% of Android devices have support for the dualSrcBlend feature (Pixel 7 with more modern graphics drivers and above). See https://vulkan.gpuinfo.org/listdevicescoverage.php?feature\u003ddualSrcBlend\u0026platform\u003dandroid ; https://vulkan.gpuinfo.org/listdevicescoverage.php?feature\u003ddualSrcBlend\u0026platform\u003dandroid\u0026option\u003dnot.\n\nFor Windows and Linux, dual src is supported in \u003e90% of devices.\n\nDifferent handling can be added for hardware that does not support it (see the workaround in https://skia.googlesource.com/skia.git/+/refs/heads/main/src/gpu/ganesh/effects/GrPorterDuffXferProcessor.cpp#371) which can be a different CL.",
